\section{Channel values}{

A handful of tokens describe a \emph{channel value} -- something bound to
data, computed, or otherwise resolved per row -- rather than one fixed R
type. Most mark encodings (\verb{x =}, \verb{y =}, \verb{fill =}, ...) accept all of
these; see \code{vignette("getting-started")} for worked examples of each.

\describe{
\item{\code{column}}{A one-sided formula naming a data column, e.g.
\code{x = ~mpg}.}
\item{\code{literal}}{A constant value applied to every row, e.g.
\code{fill = "steelblue"} or \code{opacity = 0.5}.}
\item{\code{transform()}}{A vgplotr transform function, e.g. \code{vg_bin()},
\code{vg_count()}, \code{vg_avg()} -- computed by DuckDB, not R. See
\link{vg_transforms} for the full set.}
\item{\code{sql()}/\code{agg()}}{A raw SQL expression (\code{sql()}) or one wrapping
an aggregate function (\code{agg()}), for anything a column reference or
transform can't express. See \code{\link[=sql]{sql()}}.}
\item{\code{list(value=, ...)}}{The \verb{\{value:, scale:, label:\}} object form
mosaic-spec allows for overriding a channel's scale/label directly,
e.g. \code{x = list(value = ~mpg, scale = "shared")}. Rarely needed --
the plain \code{column}/\code{literal}/\code{transform()}/\code{sql()} forms above cover
the vast majority of cases.}
}

A property whose notation includes \code{list(value=, ...)} (not just
\code{list}) is one of these \verb{\{value:, scale:, label:\}} channels; a bare
\code{list} elsewhere means an ordinary named list of sub-options specific to
that property (its own \verb{@param} text says what goes in it).
}

\section{Reactive values}{

\describe{
\item{\code{param()}}{A reactive Param or Selection, e.g.
\code{param(brush)} -- see \code{\link[=param]{param()}}. Appears on almost every argument:
mosaic-spec lets nearly any scalar option be driven by a live
\code{param()} instead of a fixed value (a slider-controlled radius, a
menu-controlled color scheme, ...), not just data-bound channels.}
}
}

